  "tarball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/github/git-sizer/tarball/v1.6.0",
  "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/github/git-sizer/zipball/v1.6.0",
  "body": "The emphasis of this release is supporting SHA-256 Git repositories, allowing arbitrary reachability roots on the command line, and rebuilding release binaries statically with Go 1.27.3.\r\n\r\n## What's new:\r\n\r\n* Add support for Git repositories using the `sha256` object format.\r\n* Allow arbitrary reachability roots (`git-sizer [OPTS] [ROOT...]`) to be specified on the command line (any revision `git rev-parse` resolves, such as `main`, `main~:src`, or an object ID). When `ROOT` arguments are given without reference selection options, only objects reachable from those roots are traversed.\r\n* Improve bare vs. worktree repository detection so `git-sizer` works when `safe.bareRepository=explicit` is set.\r\n* Avoid `git config` flags that require Git 2.18+ (`--default`, `--type=bool`, `--type=int`) for compatibility with older Git installations.\r\n\r\n## Internal changes:\r\n\r\n* Replace the internal `pipe` package with `github.com/github/go-pipe`.\r\n* Update source installation docs to use `go install` instead of `go get`.\r\n* Automate draft release creation via GitHub Actions and pin workflow actions to commit SHAs.\r\n* Disable `cgo` (`CGO_ENABLED=0`) when building release archives so Linux binaries are statically linked.\r\n* Build with the Go 1.27.3 toolchain.",
